A few comments about myth:

While it is true that "Multi-player NetHack is a myth", the opposite
does not hold. Myth is more like a multi-player rogue. It is not
nearly as large, complex, or even fun as NetHack 3.0.

Myth requires a BSD based UNIX (sockets & select) and a C++ compiler. 

I run it on sun3 and sun4c machines, compiled with g++ 1.36, g++ 1.37
and cfront 1.2. Many people seem to have trouble installing it, even
on these configurations.

The newest version can always be found on "iesd.auc.dk" (130.225.48.4)
in the directory "pub/myth". 

